WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.170
- Associate, business analyst,

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:04.790
consultant, partner, director,

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:08.220
manager, engagement manager, principal,

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.080
what do all these terms mean?

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.930
In today's video, I'm
going to explain to you

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.840
how a career in consulting looks like,

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.520
how it works and what you can expect

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.080
if you decide to join one of
these large consulting firms

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.250
like McKinsey, BCG or Bain.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:26.700
Today, I'm going to talk about,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.500
what the key career steps

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.490
in the life of an MBB
consultant looks like,

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:33.260
what you actually can expect.

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:36.830
And I trust that if you watch
this video until the very end,

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:39.010
this can really help you to understand

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:41.700
whether a career in an MBB consulting firm

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.370
is the right thing for you to do or not.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.170
Welcome to another coffee break

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:48.290
here on my channel Firm Learning.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:49.300
And on Firm Learning,

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.620
I want to help you to become successful

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.810
in the first years of your career.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:54.900
My name is Heinrich,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.867
I'm a former McKinsey consultant myself.

00:00:56.867 --> 00:00:59.490
I spent about six years with the firm

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:02.200
and in this video I really
wanna share some insights.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.950
How you can expect your
consulting career to evolve.

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.890
Let's start by demystifying

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.260
all these different
roles that are out there.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:12.240
So if you browse any career page

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:13.760
of a large consulting firm,

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.650
you will indeed see all these terms

00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:16.860
that I mentioned in the beginning.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.500
So let's break it down.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.540
And to make it easy,

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:20.373
there are pretty much

00:01:20.373 --> 00:01:22.750
only three relevant roles in consulting.

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:24.913
There's the associate role,

00:01:24.913 --> 00:01:26.800
the project lead role

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.220
and the partner role.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.620
In this video, I will go over
each of these roles in detail

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.750
and explain to you exactly
what they are all about.

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.770
But now to clear out all this confusion,

00:01:35.770 --> 00:01:37.990
let's just give you some synonymous terms

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:39.730
that are often frequently used.

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:41.507
So depending on the firm, you look like,

00:01:41.507 --> 00:01:43.240
the associate can also be called

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:45.790
business analyst, consultant,

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.330
junior or senior associate,
associate consultant,

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.720
or any other combination of these terms.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.360
What makes it even more confusing

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.850
is not only that these terms

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.680
of course, change firm by firm,

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.180
but even within the firms

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.770
there might be differences
among the different offices.

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.990
For instance at McKinsey, in many offices

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.560
there is a business analyst role, a BA,

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.460
but in Germany this does doesn't exist.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.070
The German equivalent is called a fellow,

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.930
which again doesn't exist
in most other countries.

00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:14.940
So you can see it's quite complicated

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.260
but don't get confused

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.890
it's much easier than you might think.

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:19.340
Next is the project lead.

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:22.030
And some equivalents here
are engagement manager,

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:24.927
case team lead, manager or project lead,

00:02:24.927 --> 00:02:26.860
and indeed any other variation of that.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:28.440
Again, don't get confused,

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.460
the project leader is the guy responsible

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.880
for the project on the ground.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.673
The third role is the partner role.

00:02:33.673 --> 00:02:35.970
Here some equivalents are principal,

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.930
director, senior partner,

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:40.320
junior partner, social principal

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.740
and again other variations.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:42.940
And with all of these roles,

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:45.900
these are often then also
formulated in a hierarchy, right.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.410
So maybe first you become
an associate principal,

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.780
then you become a principal

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.699
then you become a partner
or a senior partner.

00:02:51.699 --> 00:02:53.290
So of course these are order

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:55.560
but again the exact terms differ by firm.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.537
So let's start with the first
role of these three roles,

00:02:58.537 --> 00:03:00.700
and this is the associate role.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:02.770
The associate role is the first role

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.720
that you will jump in when
you start in consulting.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.850
It is the role that you will
have as a young graduate.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.140
And even most experienced hires

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:12.977
will join the MBB firms
in an associate role

00:03:12.977 --> 00:03:16.270
but of course, in a bit more
senior level within this role.

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:17.970
Associates are the ladies and gents

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:20.360
that really get their hands dirty, right?

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.860
These are the ones that will conduct

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:23.500
most of the data analysis,

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.610
these are the guys that
will really work in Excel

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:28.440
to build these models,
crunch the client data,

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:29.520
these are the people that create

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:31.370
most of the PowerPoint pages.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.170
And of course, these are the people

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:34.670
that sit together with clients

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:35.870
pretty much all day

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:37.130
having conversations with them,

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.590
conducting interviews with them,

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:41.760
collecting information that
then they try to consolidate

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.650
and synthesize for their project.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.970
In MBB firms or McKinsey, BCG or Bain,

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:48.350
you can trust that even
if you're super junior

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:50.860
as a consultant, usually
even as an intern,

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.730
you will not just be an assistant,

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:55.130
but you will always
from the very beginning,

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:58.820
be responsible for a
distinct part of the project.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:03:59.740
So there are different names

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:01.840
for that consulting
firm by consulting firm.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.350
Some call it a module,

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:04.509
other a project part,

00:04:04.509 --> 00:04:06.270
other a work-stream,

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.610
but often you try to cut,

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:08.780
in the beginning of the project

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.740
into different sub elements.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.310
And if you wanna understand this process

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.340
of structuring a project even better,

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:17.470
check out my video on
hypothesis-based problem solving,

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:18.910
I will link it somewhere above here.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:21.020
Then I will cut the project into pieces,

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:23.050
and then often you will be responsible

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.420
for one of these pieces.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.660
And now the more experience
you have in the associate role,

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.530
the higher your ranks are
within these associate roles.

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.620
Often you will be responsible for larger,

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:35.540
more complex, more complicated modules.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.740
Whereas you as a young BA

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:38.620
might start with a smaller task,

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:40.050
maybe you will be responsible

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:42.730
for a financial model that
the team needs to work on.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.300
So this is the associate role,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.990
it doesn't matter whether you are a BA,

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.650
an associate or consultant,
whatever it's called,

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.700
this is what you will do
in such an MBB project.

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:53.460
The second of the three roles

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:55.300
is the project lead role.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:58.190
So typically after two to five years

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.850
working in an associate role.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:00.990
How long exactly it takes

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.170
depends on what your
level is when you start.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:04.890
So if you start just with a bachelor,

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:05.980
it will take longer than

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:07.700
if you start as an experienced hire

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:09.564
already with an MBA or PhD.

00:05:09.564 --> 00:05:11.560
But after two to five years,

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.460
you will usually transition
into the project lead role.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:17.200
And the main transition here
is that as a project lead,

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.460
you're not only responsible

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:21.560
for a small module of work
stream of the overall project,

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:24.820
but you are responsible
for the project as a whole.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:25.760
And together with that,

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.560
of course you will be responsible

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.950
for the whole project team
that works on that project.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:33.180
A typical team size for an MBB project

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:35.690
is a team of two to five consultants.

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:36.523
So as the project lead,

00:05:36.523 --> 00:05:37.770
you will usually work together

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.350
with one to four other associates

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:42.330
that you will lead, you will guide.

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.560
So as a young project lead,

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:45.670
this would be the first
transition that you make.

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:47.370
Now, you are responsible for your team.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.330
You need to teach them,

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.470
you need to coach them.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:51.810
And of course, this can put
you also in a lot of stress

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:52.700
because now you need to

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.110
both manage upwards and manage downwards.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:57.510
Now you are the direct
contact person for the partner

00:05:57.510 --> 00:05:59.130
who will teach you to get more done

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:00.390
in a short amount of time.

00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:01.360
But at the same time,

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.960
you are also the contact
person for your associates

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.200
Who pretty much will go to you

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.650
if they believe their lifestyle

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:08.186
is not getting good enough anymore.

00:06:08.186 --> 00:06:10.470
They will ask you to reprioritize the work

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.250
and make sure they don't work too late.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:14.190
And of course you might also be confronted

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:16.870
with a whole new set of
people leadership skills.

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:18.550
So what do you do if you realize

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:21.140
that maybe one of the
associates on the team

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:22.960
is not performing to the level

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.590
that you would want them to perform?

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:25.610
How do you handle that?

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.180
How do you conduct the feedback?

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.620
How do you try to head them?

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.970
At what point do you need
to escalate the situation?

00:06:30.970 --> 00:06:33.200
So all of these are new
challenges that you're facing

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.140
that you did not face as an associate.

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:36.950
And on top of that especially in teams

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:38.750
where you only have one or two associates

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:40.910
on smaller teams, often the project lead

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:42.340
also will need to take care of

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:45.250
at least one smaller
works through for himself.

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.520
So besides all these
leadership activities,

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.440
often, there's also at least one piece

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:51.210
of very operational work

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.870
that you still need to do

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.140
and need to complete as well

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.860
just like all the other associates.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.040
So you might end up with
lots of things on your plate,

00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.480
but in the end this is indeed

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:01.250
what you need to get
done as a project lead.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.440
This is what you are responsible for.

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:05.500
Now to the third of the three roles.

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:07.230
And this is the partner role.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:10.520
So typically after two to
three years as a project lead,

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:12.830
you will advance into
the partner position.

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.410
What's important here to understand

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.130
is that most firms have a level

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:18.260
between project lead and partner.

00:07:18.260 --> 00:07:20.880
You pretty much already
do the partner role,

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.940
but you're technically
not an elected partner

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:25.270
of the firm yet.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:27.170
The main difference from the partner role

00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.600
to the project lead role,

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:30.040
is that now in the partner role

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.260
for the first time,

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.740
you're responsible for different projects

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:34.810
at the same time.

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:37.120
While the project lead
only works on one project,

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.900
the partner now needs to take care of

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:40.610
different projects in parallel.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.800
Depending on your seniority as a partner

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:45.070
and how many projects
you have in parallel,

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:46.250
the partner typically

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:47.920
is on the ground with the team

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:49.410
one or two times per week,

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:51.770
or up to one or two times per month,

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:54.080
if you are a super senior director,

00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:57.100
senior partner of the firm
that you are working for.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.430
As a partner, you are
the main contact person

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:02.000
for the board member for the senior client

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:04.240
who actually sponsored the project.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.000
In the end, the partners are the people

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.370
that pitch their projects to these people.

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.310
So they are then also responsible

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:12.780
for the project success in the very end.

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:14.610
This also means that as a partner,

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:16.301
significant share of your time

00:08:16.301 --> 00:08:19.980
will be dedicated towards
creating these pitch documents,

00:08:19.980 --> 00:08:22.110
thinking about how you could create value

00:08:22.110 --> 00:08:24.250
with new projects for your clients,

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:26.550
and then going out
conducting the pitchers,

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:29.140
wining and dining with
these senior clients

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:32.020
to make sure that your business
as a partner is growing.

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:32.853
Towards the teams,

00:08:32.853 --> 00:08:33.880
you will help them

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:37.150
with overarching guidance on the projects.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:38.880
In your portfolio of projects

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:40.450
that are going on at the same time,

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:42.464
you will often have certain projects

00:08:42.464 --> 00:08:43.790
where the team at the moment

00:08:43.790 --> 00:08:45.900
is struggling for whatever reason.

00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:46.930
You will have certain projects

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:50.470
or maybe the client at the
moment is not satisfied.

00:08:50.470 --> 00:08:52.110
So these will then be the projects,

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:54.140
or maybe you need to
invest a bit more time

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:56.480
to make sure that the
team gets back on track

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:59.630
to make sure that the demands
of the clients are met.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:01.830
Of course assuming that
these demands are feasible.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:04.100
So this is really how
the career looks like.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:07.381
You start off in the first
role, in the associate role.

00:09:07.381 --> 00:09:09.860
As an associate, your responsibilities

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.260
will increase over time

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.093
then at some point,

00:09:12.093 --> 00:09:13.800
you transition to the project lead

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:16.100
by being responsible for the whole project

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.300
for your teammates,

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:18.930
the other associates on the ground.

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:19.770
And then after that,

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:22.500
suddenly you're responsible
for a whole set of projects

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:24.780
and you are now the
person towards the client

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:26.830
who then reaches out to them, pitches them

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.620
and then is being asked to
conduct new projects for them.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:31.410
So I hope that this now demystifies

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:32.437
the career of the consultant,

00:09:32.437 --> 00:09:34.750
and I hope that this
helps you to understand

00:09:34.750 --> 00:09:36.348
whether this might be a career path

00:09:36.348 --> 00:09:38.540
that you might be interested in as well.

00:09:38.540 --> 00:09:39.550
If you have any questions

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:42.800
as always leave me a comment
below in the comment section.

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:46.200
And I will not only try to give
my very best to answer you,

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:47.360
but with every comment

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:49.000
you are also very much helping me

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.260
in supporting the channel

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:51.680
because comments and engagement

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:53.630
always look great to the YouTube systems.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:56.210
So if you took any value
out of this video at all

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:59.150
please hit the like button
